<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isma'ilism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ismaili, Ismailis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isma'ilism is a branch of Shia <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> that recognises Ismail, son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> Ja'far al-Sadiq, and his descendants as the line of imams. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> was founded on Ismaili claims and promoted the faith through missionary activity. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a> later opposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a>, and their strongholds were destroyed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> during the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>.</p></div>
